ZERO DRIVEX BAN — PASS 4
MEMORY-GROUNDED INTELLIGENCE
Architecting Intelligence Thesis Validation
You are working in the existing ZeroDriveX BAN repository.
Repository:

https://github.com/zeroday31337x/zdx-ban.git

This is BAN Pass 4.
Pass 1 established bounded multi-path reasoning.
Pass 2 established controlled paired experimental validation.
Pass 3 established measurement-grounded correctness.
Pass 4 must test and implement the central thesis from Architecting Intelligence:
Memory is not merely auxiliary context.
Memory is a substrate of intelligent behavior because current inputs acquire meaning and useful action through retained prior state, experience, structure, and outcomes.
The goal of this pass is NOT to add arbitrary “memory features.”
The goal is to construct the smallest defensible memory architecture capable of experimentally testing whether persistent, provenance-aware memory improves BAN reasoning while remaining subordinate to current measurement.
Core rule:

Memory may influence which possibilities are considered,
prioritized, recovered, or avoided.

Memory may NOT manufacture independent truth.

When memory conflicts with authoritative current
measurement, measurement wins and memory must be revised,
downgraded, or superseded.


